% A window device answers for the pixel it was asked about.
%
% GetPix is a device contract method: it reports what the page holds at
% one pixel. A device that ignored the coordinates and answered the
% ground everywhere would tell anything reading the page back -- the
% imaging machinery among them -- that the page was blank wherever it
% looked. Asking a window device this needs a display of the suite's
% own, which is why it is asked here and not with the raster devices.
%
% Three inks are laid side by side and each is read back. The colours
% are far apart on purpose: the question is whether the pixel asked
% about is the pixel answered for, so an answer that is merely the wrong
% one of the three fails as surely as the ground does.
%
% The scale is the device's: this one lays ink in 16-bit components, so
% full is 65535. What is asserted is the shape of the answer -- which
% component is full and which are empty -- and not the number, so a
% device laying ink in some other width would still be held to reporting
% the ink it laid.
%
% Runs under xvfb-run against the xcb device (see meson.build).

/failures 0 def
/check { exch { pop }{ (FAIL: ) print == /failures failures 1 add def } ifelse } bind def

1 0 0 setrgbcolor   0 0 20 30 rectfill
0 1 0 setrgbcolor  20 0 20 30 rectfill
0 0 1 setrgbcolor  40 0 20 30 rectfill

% x . [r g b]
/pix { 15 DEVICE DEVICE /GetPix get exec 3 array astore } bind def
/full { 0 get } bind def

/red   10 pix def
/green 30 pix def
/blue  50 pix def

red 0 get 0 gt   (the red fill reports ink in its first component) check
red 1 get 0 eq   (and none in its second) check
red 2 get 0 eq   (and none in its third) check

green 1 get 0 gt (the green fill reports ink in its second component) check
green 0 get 0 eq (and none in its first) check

blue 2 get 0 gt  (the blue fill reports ink in its third component) check
blue 0 get 0 eq  (and none in its first) check

failures 0 eq
    { (three inks laid and three read back: SUCCESS) = }
    { failures =print ( failures\n) print } ifelse
flush
quit
